<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Gumma</h1><p class="st-meta">1810 CE – 1902 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Gibe Oromo kingdom of south-western Ethiopia, known for its fervent Islam and for resisting incorporation into Menelik's empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gumma emerged around 1810 west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/didessa-river">Didessa</a>, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oromo">Oromo</a> groups of the region formed hereditary monarchies. It was one of five <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibe-river">Gibe</a> kingdoms, alongside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-jimma">Kingdom of Jimma</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/limmu-ennarea">Limmu-Ennarea</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gomma">Kingdom of Gomma</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gera">Kingdom of Gera</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Gumma's kings governed through appointed officials and drew revenue from farming and trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and slaves. The kingdom became known as a centre of militant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, and its rulers waged campaigns against non-Muslim neighbours. Little else is recorded in detail.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Gumma was subjected to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> in the 1880s, and after a revolt it was finally conquered and annexed in 1902.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-gumma.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Gumma" width="320" height="289"><figcaption>Image: LeGabrie · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gibe_kingdoms.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1810 CE – 1902 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oromo</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gumma</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1856&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gumma" aria-label="Kingdom of Gumma on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5692 1871 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Gumma lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6012 2127L6029 1964"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6029 1964h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6012 2127h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6012 2127h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1856&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gumma">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

